"""Buyer guidance page bodies for the local CDL Marketing review build."""


def comparison_body() -> str:
    """Return the comparison article; the caller supplies its hero and CTA."""
    return '''<section class="section"><article class="wrap article-layout" aria-label="CDL Marketing and Broadlume comparison">
<p class="article-meta">Reviewed <time datetime="2026-11-04">November 4, 2026</time> · Published by CDL Marketing</p>
<p class="answer">Considering a Broadlume alternative? Compare the work your showroom needs, the systems you already use and the terms in each proposal. Broadlume, now a Cyncly company, offers a broad flooring technology platform. CDL brings an operator's perspective to a focused marketing engagement.</p>

<h2>Where Broadlume and Cyncly are strong</h2>
<p>Cyncly's flooring website packages list product catalogs, sample ordering, visualization, reporting, call tracking and reputation tools. Higher tiers add Retail Lead Management seats, an account manager and additional marketing services. Its <a href="https://www.cyncly.com/products/cyncly-websites/flooring">current package table</a> explains those distinctions.</p>
<p>Broadlume also advertises <a href="https://www.broadlume.com/products/websites/seo">flooring-specific SEO</a>, including content, local listings and backlinks. Cyncly's <a href="https://www.cyncly.com/resources/blog/ai-changes-for-living-spaces-retail">October 2026 guidance on AI and showroom shopping</a> discusses AI answer engines and connecting online exploration to customer inquiries. These are real parts of its published offer and positioning.</p>

<h2>What CDL brings to the decision</h2>
<p>We run flooring showrooms ourselves. That experience shapes how we approach a homeowner's search, product questions and first contact with the store. <a href="/about/">Meet the people behind CDL</a> and the businesses that inform our work.</p>
<p>Our current offer centers on <a href="/services/local-seo/">local SEO</a>, <a href="/services/paid-ads/">paid advertising</a>, <a href="/services/websites/">showroom websites</a> and <a href="/services/ai-search/">AI search visibility</a>. We agree on the work before starting. CRM integration is planned for later and is not available in our current offer.</p>

<h2>Compare the proposals side by side</h2>
<div class="tbl" role="region" aria-label="Comparison of CDL Marketing and Broadlume or Cyncly published offers" tabindex="0">
<table class="pricing-table"><caption>Questions for a flooring marketing agency comparison</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Buyer question</th><th scope="col">CDL Marketing</th><th scope="col">Broadlume / Cyncly</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">What am I buying?</th><td>A scoped marketing service informed by showroom operating experience.</td><td>A flooring website and technology offering with feature tiers and additional services.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">What happens to my current systems?</th><td>We assess the website and marketing access needed. CRM integration is future work.</td><td>Packages list connected website tools and RLM seats. Confirm compatibility with your specific systems.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">What will I pay?</th><td>Review <a href="/pricing/">pricing</a> and your written scope. Advertising spend and service fees are separate.</td><td>The reviewed package table has no dollar rates. Request a proposal for the equivalent scope.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Who controls the accounts, and how do I leave?</th><td>Confirm access, ownership, cancellation and handover terms in your agreement.</td><td>These contract terms were not established by this public-page review. Ask for the applicable agreement.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<div class="callout"><h3>Compare evidence, too</h3><p>A service list describes an offer. It does not establish your likely results. Ask each provider for relevant examples, measurement definitions and the limits of its evidence. CDL's operating experience is not a verified client-results history.</p></div>

<h2>Make the next step useful</h2>
<p>Bring your website, current provider scope and the problem you want solved. We can discuss whether CDL's marketing services fit. Our <a href="/guides/choosing-a-flooring-marketing-agency/">agency buying guide</a> gives you questions to use with any provider.</p>
<p>This is CDL's comparison of public information, not an independent product trial. Features and terms can change. Broadlume's <a href="https://www.broadlume.com/terms-of-use">website-use terms</a> say purchased software has separate terms, so they do not settle a dealer's commercial contract. <a href="/contact/">Talk through your showroom's needs</a>.</p>
</article></section>'''


def agency_guide_body() -> str:
    """Return the buying guide article; the caller supplies its hero and CTA."""
    return '''<section class="section"><article class="wrap article-layout" aria-label="Guide to choosing a flooring marketing agency">
<p class="article-meta">By CDL Marketing · <time datetime="2026-11-04">November 4, 2026</time></p>
<p class="answer">Choose a flooring marketing agency by the work it will do, the evidence behind its recommendations and the terms you can review. Start with your showroom's problem: getting found, making the website useful or reaching more local shoppers.</p>

<h2>Eight questions before you hire</h2>
<ol>
<li><h3>What will you do for my showroom?</h3><p>Ask for specific deliverables, locations covered, responsibilities and exclusions. Separate <a href="/services/local-seo/">local SEO</a>, <a href="/services/paid-ads/">ads</a> and <a href="/services/websites/">website work</a>. A broad service label is not a work plan.</p></li>
<li><h3>Do you understand how flooring is sold?</h3><p>Discuss products, service areas, installation questions and how customers request a measure. Ask for relevant experience. Our <a href="/about/">showroom operating background</a> informs our approach, but experience alone does not prove client results.</p></li>
<li><h3>What does the full bill include?</h3><p>Request separate lines for platform or hosting fees, agency management, setup, content and advertising spend. Ask what changes the price and which optional tools cost extra. Compare the same scope across proposals.</p></li>
<li><h3>What proof can you show?</h3><p>Ask for examples with dates, starting conditions, work completed and spend context. Check whether a result means inquiries, booked measures, sold jobs or collected revenue. A percentage without a baseline can hide more than it explains.</p></li>
<li><h3>Who controls the website and accounts?</h3><p>Confirm domain registration, hosting, content rights, administrator access and control of ad and analytics accounts. Put cancellation, export, handover and any transfer charges in writing before signing.</p></li>
<li><h3>What access will you need?</h3><p>Agree on website, business-profile and advertising permissions. If CRM access or integration is proposed, identify the supported connection, data involved, owner and testing plan. Ask what happens if that connection is unavailable.</p></li>
<li><h3>How will we know what is working?</h3><p>Agree on a qualified inquiry and which outcomes you can reliably record. Ask to see a sample report that explains findings, missing data and next actions. Calls and forms should not automatically be counted as sales.</p></li>
<li><h3>What can you reasonably promise?</h3><p>Ask what the agency controls and what depends on your market, access and staff. Be cautious about guaranteed rankings or AI recommendations. <a href="/services/ai-search/">AI search work</a> should have a concrete scope, just like other marketing.</p></li>
</ol>

<h2>A practical first 90 days</h2>
<p>Use this as a review framework, with timing agreed around access and scope:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>First month:</strong> establish the starting picture, confirm access and measurement, agree priorities and fix the most useful basics.</li>
<li><strong>Second month:</strong> carry out the agreed campaigns or content work and check the contact paths. Review actual inquiry quality with your team.</li>
<li><strong>Third month:</strong> compare results with the starting picture, explain limitations and decide what to improve next. Organic visibility may need sustained work beyond this period.</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout"><h3>Leave with something you can review</h3><p>Before committing, get a written scope, itemized costs, access responsibilities and review plan. At CDL, marketing is the current service. CRM integration is planned for later and is not available today.</p></div>
<p><a href="/pricing/">Review our pricing</a>, <a href="/compare/broadlume/">compare CDL with Broadlume / Cyncly</a> or <a href="/contact/">discuss your showroom</a>.</p>
</article></section>'''
